% ====================================================
% REPEAT — Isaiah 65:17–25
% Source: black ink, photo 51 (PXL_20261105_235925779.jpg); the page has the
%   teacher's red check mark at 65:17.
% Compare with: Isaiah/65.tex (blue ink, photo 46)
% ====================================================
  \pa \verse{65:17} For behold, He created a new heaven and a new earth.%%

  \pa He won't remember\alt{mention} things as they were\alt{former things},\pa neither will they come to mind.%%

  \pa \verse{65:18} Rather, rejoice and be glad\pa in that which I create.%%

  \pa For behold, I created Jerusalem\pa and her people rejoice.%%

  \pa \verse{65:19} I will rejoice over Jerusalem\pa and will have joy in\alt{because of} My people.%%

  \pa The sound of weeping shall no longer be heard in her,\pa neither the voice of crying.%%

  \pa \verse{65:20} There shall no longer be from there\pa an infant of days,%%

  \pa neither an old man who has not completed\pa his days.%%

  \pa For the youth shall die at 100\pa and the 100-year-old sinner shall be cursed.\ed{How so?}%%

  \pa \verse{65:21} They shall build houses and live in them.\pa They will plant vineyards and eat the fruit thereof.%%

  \pa \verse{65:22} They shall not build and another inhabit,\pa neither plant and another eat,%%

  \pa because the days of a tree shall be the days of My people,\pa and Mine elect shall long enjoy the fruits of their labors,\alt{the work of their hands,}%%

  \pa their workmanship.%
  \ed{This had to be comforting for the pioneers.}%%

  \pa \verse{65:23} They shall not labor in vain,\pa neither give birth in terror.%%

  \pa For they are the blessed posterity\alt{seed} of the \lord\pa and their offspring with them.%%

  \pa \verse{65:24} So shall it be that I will answer before they call;\pa I will hear\alt{listen, heed, understand} even while they are speaking.%%

  \pa \verse{65:25} The wolf and the lamb shall feed together;\pa the lion will eat straw like the ox.%%

  \pa The serpent's meat\ed{singular} will be dust.%
  \ed{``Dust from shall eat''? with a circled \Hebrew{ת}}%%

  \pa Nothing will hurt or destroy\pa in all My holy mountain, says the \lord.%%
